---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ScrollReveal from '../components/ScrollReveal.jsx';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Sean Winslow" description="The story of a creative who learned to think like a product manager.">
  <ScrollReveal client:visible>

    <!-- About Hero -->
    <section class="reveal-section about-hero-section">
      <h1 class="about-title">
        About
      </h1>
      <p class="about-subtitle">
        A creative who learned to think in systems.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Chapter 1: The Artist -->
    <section class="reveal-section about-chapter-section">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="about-chapter-text">
          <div class="about-chapter-label">Chapter 1</div>
          <h2 class="about-chapter-h2">
            The Artist
          </h2>
          <div class="about-body-stack">
            <p class="about-body">
              For twelve years, I was a freelance creative in New York City. Illustration, animation, film — if it involved telling a visual story, I was in. I worked with agencies, startups, and independent filmmakers, building a career around the belief that craft and clarity of communication are the same thing.
            </p>
            <p class="about-body">
              Those years taught me something that would later prove invaluable: every creative project is a product problem in disguise. Who is the audience? What do they need to feel? What's the constraint? What's the deadline? I was doing product thinking without knowing the vocabulary.
            </p>
            <p class="about-body">
              The animation work, in particular, built a muscle for systems thinking. When you're managing a 2D animation pipeline — storyboards, keyframes, in-betweens, compositing, sound design — you're managing dependencies, critical paths, and quality gates. You're running sprints, even if you don't call them that.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="about-image-placeholder">
          <span class="about-placeholder-text">Illustration / Animation Work</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Divider -->
    <div class="about-divider-wrap">
      <div class="about-divider"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- Chapter 2: The Pivot -->
    <section class="reveal-section about-chapter-section">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="about-chapter-text">
          <div class="about-chapter-label">Chapter 2</div>
          <h2 class="about-chapter-h2">
            The Pivot
          </h2>
          <div class="about-body-stack">
            <p class="about-body">
              In 2024, I made a deliberate career shift. The AI wave wasn't just changing creative work — it was redefining what it meant to build products. I recognized that the most impactful role in this new landscape wasn't the person drawing the frames, but the person deciding which frames to draw and why.
            </p>
            <p class="about-body">
              I invested in PM education — courses, certifications, and most importantly, building. I created Pocket PM, a GPT-powered product management assistant, as both a learning exercise and a proof of concept. It forced me to think about API design, user research, and feature prioritization from the builder's seat.
            </p>
            <p class="about-body">
              The pivot wasn't a departure from creativity — it was an evolution. Product management is creative problem-solving with constraints. The medium changed; the mindset didn't.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="about-image-placeholder">
          <span class="about-placeholder-text">Pocket PM / Career Transition</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Divider -->
    <div class="about-divider-wrap">
      <div class="about-divider"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- Chapter 3: The Builder -->
    <section class="reveal-section about-chapter-section">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="about-chapter-text">
          <div class="about-chapter-label">Chapter 3</div>
          <h2 class="about-chapter-h2">
            The Builder
          </h2>
          <div class="about-body-stack">
            <p class="about-body">
              Landing at The Block as Associate PM gave me the platform to merge both worlds. My first major project — Campus 201 — was an education platform redesign that required exactly the kind of dual fluency I'd been building: the creative intuition to understand how people learn, and the technical rigor to ship a product at scale.
            </p>
            <p class="about-body">
              In parallel, I've been building systems. The Superuser Pack — a Claude Code command center with 106 custom skills — emerged from my belief that PMs should be able to prototype, automate, and build without waiting for engineering cycles. The Animation Pipeline project applies AI to my original discipline, creating a production system that could democratize 2D animation.
            </p>
            <p class="about-body">
              This is who I am now: someone who thinks in systems, builds with intention, and brings a creative sensibility to every product decision. The artist didn't disappear — the artist learned to scale.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="about-image-placeholder">
          <span class="about-placeholder-text">The Block / Builder Setup</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!--
      IMAGE SWIPER — Future Integration
      Stacked card deck (9 art-style portraits) with drag-to-reveal interaction.
      Reference implementation: sw-old-portfolio/Sean_Winslow_Personal_Portfolio-OLD/Sean-Winslow-Portfolio/src/components/ui/ImageSwiper.jsx
      Spec: design-system-spec.md section 15 "Carried-Forward Feature: Image Swiper"
      Cards: 360x480px, CSS perspective(700px), 50px drag threshold, 300ms transitions.
      Place between Chapter 3 and the spacer as a standalone interactive section.
    -->

    <!-- Spacer -->
    <div class="about-spacer"></div>

  </ScrollReveal>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  /* Hero */
  .about-hero-section {
    padding: var(--space-32) var(--space-6) var(--space-16);
    max-width: var(--text-max-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .about-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-display);
    line-height: var(--text-display-lh);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .about-subtitle {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
    line-height: var(--text-h3-lh);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Chapter sections */
  .about-chapter-section {
    padding: var(--space-16) var(--space-6);
    max-width: var(--content-max-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* Grid — single column by default, two columns on wider screens */
  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-10);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .about-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .about-chapter-text {
    max-width: var(--text-max-width);
  }

  .about-chapter-label {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .about-chapter-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    line-height: var(--text-h2-lh);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .about-body-stack {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .about-body {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: var(--text-body-lh);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Image placeholder */
  .about-image-placeholder {
    aspect-ratio: 4/3;
    background-color: var(--surface-2);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--surface-3);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 280px;
  }

  .about-placeholder-text {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  /* Divider */
  .about-divider-wrap {
    max-width: var(--text-max-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-6);
  }

  .about-divider {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--surface-3);
  }

  /* Bottom spacer */
  .about-spacer {
    height: var(--space-16);
  }
</style>
